---
layout: base.njk
title: Data & Visual Tools
description: The datasets behind the site, where they come from, and how they are checked before publication.
---

{% include "shapes.njk" %}

<div class="wrap">

  <div class="page-head">
    <p class="eyebrow">Behind the charts</p>
    <h1>Data &amp; Visual Tools</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Every chart on this site is built from a spreadsheet kept alongside the code.
      Nothing is typed into a page by hand, so a chart can never drift out of step
      with the data it claims to show.
    </p>
  </div>

  <section class="card" aria-labelledby="ds-heading">
    <h2 id="ds-heading" style="font-size:1.075rem">Datasets</h2>

    <div class="grid grid-2" style="margin-top:1rem">
      <div class="stat" style="padding:1rem">
        <div class="stat-label">Timeline</div>
        <div class="stat-value">{{ timeline.events | length }} events</div>
        <p class="small muted" style="margin:0.5rem 0 0">
          {{ timeline.categories | length }} tracks · {{ timeline.minYear | formatYear }}&ndash;{{ timeline.maxYear | formatYear }}<br>
          Source: <code>data/{{ timeline.source }}</code>{% if timeline.sheet %} · sheet <code>{{ timeline.sheet }}</code>{% endif %}
          {% if timeline.updated %}<br>Updated <time datetime="{{ timeline.updated | isoDate }}">{{ timeline.updated | humanDate }}</time>{% endif %}
        </p>
        <p style="margin:0.7rem 0 0"><a href="{{ '/timeline/' | url }}">View the timeline &rarr;</a></p>
      </div>

      <div class="stat" style="padding:1rem">
        <div class="stat-label">Tracks</div>
        <div style="margin-top:0.5rem;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0.3rem">
          {% for cat in timeline.categories %}
          <span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:0.45rem;font-size:0.875rem">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" width="13" height="13"
                 style="flex:none;fill: var(--s{{ cat.colorIndex + 1 }})">
              <use href="#shape-{{ cat.shape }}"></use>
            </svg>
            {{ cat.name }}
            <span class="muted" style="font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums">{{ cat.count }}</span>
          </span>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card" style="margin-top:1.25rem" aria-labelledby="how-heading">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2 id="how-heading" style="font-size:1.075rem;margin-top:0">How the data gets here</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>The data lives at <code>data/timeline.csv</code> in the repository.</li>
        <li>A build step reads it, checks every date, and writes plain JSON.</li>
        <li>The site is rebuilt from that JSON and published.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        Steps 2 and 3 run automatically whenever the data changes, so updating a
        chart means editing one file and committing it. Readers only ever download
        the finished JSON — the parser stays on the build machine.
      </p>
      <p>
        Suggestions from readers join at step 1: they arrive for review, and an
        approved entry is written into the same file by the same checks.
        <a href="{{ '/submit/' | url }}">Suggest an entry &rarr;</a>
      </p>

      <h2 style="font-size:1.075rem">Columns the timeline understands</h2>
      <p>Headings are matched loosely, so <code>Start Year</code>, <code>start_year</code> and <code>YEAR</code> all work.</p>
      <div class="table-scroll">
        <table class="data" style="min-width:34rem">
          <thead>
            <tr><th scope="col">Column</th><th scope="col">Required</th><th scope="col">Notes</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><th scope="row">Category</th><td>Yes</td><td>Becomes a track. Also accepts Type, Track, Theme.</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Event</th><td>Yes</td><td>The label. Also accepts Title, Name, Milestone.</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Start</th><td>Yes</td><td><code>1948</code>, <code>1948-07-29</code>, <code>July 1948</code>, <code>776 BC</code>, <code>AD 79</code>, or <code>c. 3000 BC</code> when approximate.</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">End</th><td>No</td><td>Present means the event draws as a bar rather than a point.</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Detail</th><td>No</td><td>The tooltip body. Also accepts Tooltip, Description, Note.</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Location</th><td>No</td><td>Shown in the tooltip and the table.</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Link</th><td>No</td><td>Makes the event clickable through to a source.</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Highlight</th><td>No</td><td><code>yes</code> keeps the label visible when a lane gets crowded.</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <p class="small muted">
        A companion file, <code>data/categories.csv</code>, pins each track's group,
        colour and marker shape so they stay stable as rows are added. Colour
        identifies the group; shape identifies the track within it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

</div>
